Found in the k210 review (branch k210-211). langertha-skeid lib/Langertha/Skeid/Protocol/Anthropic.pm:136 calls Langertha::Tool->from_list($body->{tools}) on client-sent Anthropic tools inside request_to_openai, which Proxy.pm:320 (_handle_anthropic_messages) calls with no eval. Since k210, a client that sends an Anthropic built-in (web_search_20250305, bash_20250124, text_editor_*, computer_*, mcp_toolset, ...) makes from_list croak, and Mojolicious answers 500 text/html (reproduced with Mojolicious::Lite, production mode). No Anthropic-shaped error JSON, no usage event, and it looks like a gateway fault. Before k210 the built-in was silently turned into a function tool, so the fail-loud direction is right; the status code and shape are wrong. Proposal: core exposes a public non-croaking classifier, e.g. Langertha::Tool->classify($hash) returning function | server:<wire> | unsupported:<type>, or at least is_function_tool($hash) plus a public server_tool_wire (ResponsesCompatible already calls the private _server_tool_wire across packages). skeid then answers 400 invalid_request_error naming the tool, or strips it with a warning header by policy. The skeid-side change belongs on the skeid board once the core API lands.

2026-09-25 02:39 Core side landed on branch k210-211 (bc1e8ee): Langertha::Tool->classify($hash, $fmt) is public and never croaks. Scalar: function | server | client_builtin | foreign (only with $fmt: a built-in of another wire) | unknown (unrecognised type, no type and no name, or not a hash). List context: ($category, $wire, $label) where wire is responses/anthropic/gemini for built-ins and label is the type, Gemini key, or the keys of a nameless hash. from_hash/from_list/format_list croak on every category but function, from the same classifier. Skeid mapping: before Tool->from_list in Protocol/Anthropic.pm request_to_openai, run classify($_, 'anthropic') over body->{tools}; any non-function -> 400 {type:error, error:{type:invalid_request_error, message:'tool <label> (<category>) is not supported by this gateway'}} (or strip by policy). No skeid change made from core.

